# BMW Ride Planner -- environment
#
# Copy to .env and fill in only what you need:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# NOTHING here is required for the core app. Everything the demo does today runs
# with no keys at all: the routing graph comes from BMW's own dataset, and
# Open-Meteo needs no key. The entries below are all optional upgrades.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- dataset path
# Where the BMW hackathon dataset lives. Only set this if it is not in the
# default location.
# BMW_DATASET=/home/krishaanth/Desktop/BMW/exd_download/datasetHackathon

# ------------------------------------------------------------- no key required
# Open-Meteo forecast + archive. No signup, no key. Already wired up.
#   https://open-meteo.com
# OpenStreetMap via Overpass or a Geofabrik extract. No key.
#   https://download.geofabrik.de/europe/germany/bayern.html
# Copernicus DEM GLO-30 on AWS open data. No key.
# German Unfallatlas accident data. No key, direct download.

# ------------------------------------------------------- optional: live traffic
# The ONLY thing in the whole design that needs a key, and it is optional. The
# default congestion model is derived from BMW's own 85,699 trips (median speed
# per segment per time band), which needs no network. A live layer only adds
# what the prior genuinely cannot know: today's closures, incidents and
# roadworks.
#
# Pick ONE if you want it. Free tiers are sufficient.
#   HERE     -> https://platform.here.com   (Traffic API v7)
#   TomTom   -> https://developer.tomtom.com (Traffic Flow + Incidents)
# HERE_API_KEY=
# TOMTOM_API_KEY=

# ------------------------------------------------- optional: basemap tiles
# Leaflet falls back to CARTO and then plain OSM when these are absent, so the
# map always draws. Set them for terrain and outdoor styles, which are what a
# ride planner actually wants under a route line.
#   Stadia   -> https://stadiamaps.com     (outdoors, terrain, dark)
#              browser keys are Referer-scoped: add your origin in their console
#   Geoapify -> https://geoapify.com       (dark-matter, osm-bright)
# STADIA_API_KEY=
# GEOAPIFY_API_KEY=

# ------------------------------------------- optional: Copernicus CLMS download
# Land cover (CORINE) needs a free account to DOWNLOAD the raster, but not to
# use it afterwards. Currently deferred -- OSM landuse covers most of it.
# CLMS_USERNAME=
# CLMS_PASSWORD=
